Here's some information taken from the dungeon/level description files and
translated into understandable text.  If you don't want to read Spoilers about
the locations of special levels and such in the typical Nethack dungeon,
read no further.

  What do you want to read? [hij or ?*] h
  As you read the article, it disappears.--More--

  Suddenly, a map coalesces in your mind!

The main dungeon is 25-30 levels deep.
  An extra down-stairwell on a level from 2 to 5 leads to The Gnomish Mines.
  The Oracle level always appears between levels 5 and 10.
  The Bigroom occurs 15% of the time, between levels 10 and 13.
  The Rogue-style level always appears between levels 15 and 19.
     (presumably this will never be the level with either magic portal)
  A magic portal to The Quest appears 6-8 levels below the Oracle level.
     (effectively anywhere between levels 11 and 18)
  A magic portal to Fort Ludios appears between levels 18 and 22.
     (the portal will be inside a Magic Memory Vault)
  The Medusa level appears no more than 5 levels from the bottom.
     (Code indicates possibility of 2 Medusa levels.)
     (effectively anywhere from 20 to 29)
  The Castle level always appears on the bottom level of the dungeon.
     (effectively anywhere from 25 to 30)

The Gnomish Mines are 8-10 levels deep.  (Top level is 'M1')
  The Mine Town appears between levels M3 and M5.
     It will always have a Candle Shop.
     90% chance each of a Tool, Food, and one random Shop.
  The bottom of the mine appears between levels M8 and M10 (according to
     the depth of the mine, of course) and has no down-staircase.
     A secret alcove contains 2 diamonds, 3 emeralds, 2 rubies, 2
     amethysts, a Luckstone, and 7 other random gem-types.

The Oracle, Bigroom, and Rogue-style levels are only one level in size, with
  no reliable treasures of significance.

The Quest is 5-7 levels high.  (It goes up, not down.  Bottom is 'Q1'.)
  The first level, in theory, could be repeated again on the next level.
  A special level appears on Q3.
  Your goal is at the top, Q5-Q7.  So's the Silver Bell of Opening.
  The other levels are just "filler".

Fort Ludios is only one level in size.  Its corners always contain 12 valuable
  gems (3 diamonds, 3 emeralds, 3 rubies, and 3 amethysts).

The Medusa level(s) contain no reliable treasures of significance.

The Castle always has a Wand of Wishing, and four rooms filled with various
  equipment (Armor, Weapons, Gems, and Food.)

Vlad's Tower is 3 levels high.  (It goes up, not down.  Bottom is 'V1'.)
  Level V1 always has a Long Sword, a Lock Pick, an Elven Cloak, and a
    Blindfold.  They're always on trapped spaces, as well.
  There's an Amulet of Life Saving on V2.  There is also an Amulet of
    Strangulation, Water Walking Boots, a Crystal Plate Mail, and a Spellbook
    of Invisibility.
  Vlad is on V3, with the Candelabrum of Invocation.

Gehennom (Hell) starts on the level below the Castle, and goes down
25-30 levels, just like the main dungeon.  Henceforth, this level is called
G1, for 'Gehennom 1st'.
  The Valley of Death is always the first level of Gehennom.  (G1)
  Asmodeus's level appears between G2 and G8.
  Juiblex's level appears between G6 and G10.
  Baalzebub's level appears between G9 and G13.
  An extra up-stairwell leads to Vlad's Tower, between levels G13 and G18.
  Orcus's level appears between G15 and G20.
  The top level of the Wizard's Tower appears between G15 and G21.
     (The 2nd and 3rd levels of the Wizard's Tower are immediately below.)
  Two fake Wizard levels appear, 1-5 levels from the bottom of Gehennom.
     The completely worthless one will have an amulet in the center.
     The other one has a portal to the Wizard's Tower (lvl 3) in the center.
     (effectively between G20 and G29)
  The vibrating space to enter Moloch's Sanctum is always on the next-to-last
     level of Gehennom.  (effectively G24 to G29)
  Moloch's Sanctum is always the bottom level of Gehennom.
     (effectively anywhere from G25 to G30)

Details of the Wizard's Tower, Moloch's Sanctum, and the Endgame are for you
to discover on your own.  (The Book of the Dead is in the Wizard's Tower.)

